    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0373" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.7962/51: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-03T09:00:00-00:44">March 3, 1942—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. From McBride. Am sending today as number 55<anchor n="10" xml:id="d428-f1"/>
                    in five sections text of proposed agreement between Liberia and the United
                    States covering military use of airports and defense areas in Liberia. It
                    follows agreement with Greenland<anchor n="11" xml:id="d428-f2"/> with
                    modifications appropriate to Liberian situation. It was worked out in
                    consultation with President Barclay who approves this text.</p>
                <p>Under Liberian procedure, agreement must be submitted to Liberian Senate for
                    approval and will therefore probably become public. Barclay informs me Senate
                    will take prompt action.</p>
                <p>It will be appreciated if Department will let me have any comment or suggested
                    changes either as to form or content as soon as feasible. I should like to
                    conclude matter before leaving Monrovia if possible.</p>
                <p>Will it be expedient to publish this agreement in the United States? Have I
                    necessary authorization to sign for the United States?</p>
                <pb facs="0374" n="362" xml:id="pg362"/>
                <p>After agreement signed I would send confidential letter to Barclay embodying
                    specific items of assistance. Letter would first be submitted to Department.
                    [McBride.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wharton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
